 it should be placed in tasks/main.yml. No hosts or vars sections are needed since it\'s a role-specific playbook.\n\nDouble-checking each task to ensure the module names and parameters are correct. For example, using apt_repository for adding the Docker repo and apt_key for managing keys. Also, ensuring that the notify is correctly pointing to the apt_cache_update handler.\n\nFinally, I\'ll write out the YAML, making sure it starts with \'---\' and each task is properly indented and structured without any comments or explanations, as per the user\'s instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure apt key is not present in trusted.gpg.d\n  apt_key:\n    key: /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/docker.gpg\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure old apt source list is not present in /etc/apt/sources.list.d\n  file:\n    path: /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list\n    state: absent\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Ensure old versions of Docker are not installed.\n  apt:\n    name: docker-engine\n    state: absent\n    purge: yes\n    autoremove: yes\n\n- name: Ensure legacy repo file is not present.\n  file:\n    path: /etc/yum.repos.d/docker.repo\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure dependencies are installed.\n  apt:\n    name: [apt-transport-https, ca-certificates]\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Add or remove Docker repository\n  apt_repository:\n    repo: "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/docker-archive-keyring.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu jammy stable"\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Ensure handlers are notified immediately to update the apt cache\n  apt:\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n  become: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T07:50:09.317180731Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12746947941, 'load_duration': 90711092, 'prompt_eval_count': 439, 'prompt_eval_duration': 98951073, 'eval_count': 8