 change the module to \'ansible.builtin.shell\' and set \'changed_when: false\'. That way, the task won\'t report as changed unless the command actually does something.\n\nSo I\'ll update the second task: replace \'ansible.builtin.command\' with \'ansible.builtin.shell\' and add \'changed_when: false\'. Also, I\'ll make sure the command is properly quoted to avoid shell injection issues, but in this case, it\'s safe.\n\nLet me structure the corrected task. The name stays the same, the module changes to \'ansible.builtin.shell\', and I add \'changed_when: false\'. The command remains \'pkill -u ansible\'.\n\nI think that should fix the linting error because now the task won\'t change the state unless the command affects something, and it won\'t run unnecessarily.\n\nI\'ll make sure the playbook starts with \'---\' and each task is correctly formatted. The first task seems fine, so I\'ll leave it as is.\n\nSo the corrected playbook will have the first task as before and the second task modified with the new module and parameters.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure docker users are added to the docker group\n  ansible.builtin.user:\n    name: "{{ user_name }}"\n    group: docker\n    state: present\n    groups: [docker]\n\n- name: Reset ssh connection to apply user changes\n  ansible.builtin.shell:\n    cmd: pkill -u ansible\n    changed_when: false\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T07:57:46.369790723Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13319649115, 'load_duration': 90229247, 'prompt_eval_count': 1031, 'prompt_eval_duration': 354198001, 'eval_count': 744, 'eval_duration': 12874394527, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7b1aeba0-4c05-4bec-87ac-8d98dd52dc75-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1031, 'output_tokens': 744, 'total_tokens': 1775}
