asks:\' list.\n\nSo the correct structure should be:\n\n---\ntasks:\n  - name: Task 1: Enable modules\n    community.general.apache2_module:\n      state: enabled\n      modules: [\'modules\']\n\n  - name: Task 2: Configure locations\n    ansible.builtin.template:\n      src: "apache.conf.j2"\n      dest: "/etc/apache2/apache2.conf"\n\nAh, that makes sense. The user\'s last generated playbook didn\'t include the \'tasks:\' key, which is why yamllint was complaining about mapping values not allowed. The \'tasks\' are a list, and without the key, YAML gets confused about the structure.\n\nSo the fix is to add \'tasks:\' and indent the tasks under it. That should resolve the syntax error.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\ntasks:\n  - name: Task 1: Enable modules\n    community.general.apache2_module:\n      state: enabled\n      modules: [\'modules\']\n\n  - name: Task 2: Configure locations\n    ansible.builtin.template:\n      src: "apache.conf.j2"\n      dest: "/etc/apache2/apache2.conf"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T08:47:18.847623771Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11774063691, 'load_duration': 108084024, 'prompt_eval_count': 422, 'prompt_eval_duration': 6761522, 'eval_count': 672, 'eval_duration': 11658489203, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--bf9f7117-396e-41f2-bd88-90105dd12c25-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 422, 'output_tokens': 672, 'total_tokens': 1094}
