content='<think>\nOkay, so I\'ve been given a list of tasks that need to be converted into an Ansible Playbook. Let me go through each task one by one to make sure I understand what\'s needed.\n\nFirst, the Playbook has to start with \'---\' on the very first line. That\'s straightforward. I\'ll make sure that\'s the case.\n\nLooking at Task 1, I need to check if Python is installed. The command module is perfect for this. I\'ll use the shell command \'which python\' and store the output in the variable python_executable. But wait, I should think about what happens if Python isn\'t installed. The command might fail, so maybe I should handle that, but the task just says to check and store the result, so I\'ll proceed as instructed.\n\nTask 2 is similar but for Python3. I\'ll use \'which python3\' and store it in python3_executable.\n\nNext, Tasks 3 and 4 are about debugging. I\'ll use the debug module to print the paths. For Task 3, I\'ll output python_executable.stdout, and for Task 4, python3_executable.stdout.\n\nTask 5 is about importing assert.yml. I\'ll use the import_tasks module pointing to that file. Since it\'s a relative path, I\'ll make sure the role\'s structure includes it.\n\nFor Task 6, I need to install packages using the package module. The variable openssl_requirements will hold the package names. I\'ll use the state=present to ensure they\'re installed.\n\nTask 7 ensures that \'dnf\' is available for packaging. Using the package module with name=dnf and state=present should do it.\n\nTask 8 is about installing pip packages. The pip module will be used with the requirements from openssl_pip_packages. I\'ll set state=present to install them.\n\nNow, Tasks 9, 10, and 11 involve creating directories for keys, csr, and crt respectively. I\'ll use the file module with state=directory. Each will specify their respective directory variables and set the owner, group, and mode as needed.\n\nFinally, Task 12 requires including create.yml using include_tasks. I\'ll loop over the openssl_items variable and set the label with item.name. This means each iteration will process a different task from create.yml.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are in the correct order as specified. Also, each task should have the exact module names and parameters as instructed. I\'ll avoid adding any extra comments or explanations since the output should be a clean YAML file.\n\nI should also ensure that the Playbook adheres to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. That means proper indentation, correct use of colons, and no trailing spaces. Since this is for an Ansible Role, the tasks should be in the tasks/main.yml file, so the structure should be correct.\n\nWait, for the command module, if the executable isn\'t found, the command will fail. Maybe I should set ignore_errors to True, but the task doesn\'t specify that, so I\'ll leave it as is. The user might want the play to fail if Python isn\'t installed, which is a valid use case.\n\nFor the file module tasks, I should ensure that the directories are created with the correct ownership and permissions. Using owner, group, and mode parameters will handle that.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all tasks. Now, I\'ll structure them in the Playbook, making sure each task follows the previous one without any skips or misplacements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if python is installed\n  command: which python\n  register: python_executable\n\n- name: Check if python3 is installed\n  command: which python3\n  register: python3_executable\n\n- name: Debug Python executable path\n  debug:\n    msg: "Python executable path is: {{ python_executable.stdout }}"\n\n- name: Debug Python3 executable path\n  debug:\n    msg: "Python3 executable path is: {{ python3_executable.stdout }}"\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install requirements\n  package:\n    name: "{{ openssl_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Ensure packaging is available via dnf\n  package:\n    name: dnf\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install pip packages\n  pip:\n    requirements: "{{ openssl_pip_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create key directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ openssl_key_directory }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ openssl_file_owner }}"\n    group: "{{ openssl_file_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create csr directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ openssl_csr_directory }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ openssl_file_owner }}"\n    group: "{{ openssl_file_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create crt directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ openssl_crt_directory }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ openssl_file_owner }}"\n    group: "{{ openssl_file_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Include create.yml\n  include_tasks: create.yml\n  loop: "{{ openssl_items }}"\n  loop_control:\n    loop_var: item\n    label: "{{ item.name }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T08:58:17.657796629Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 19885299564, 'load_duration': 83953000, 'prompt_eval_count': 703, 'prompt_eval_duration': 346106984, 'eval_count': 1105, 'eval_duration': 19453830994, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--b3b93c38-2e5a-4fe1-92dc-642d144e309f-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 703, 'output_tokens': 1105, 'total_tokens': 1808}
