n\nLet me structure each task with the correct YAML syntax, making sure the indentation and keys are properly formatted. I\'ll use the \'ansible.builtin\' module paths as required by Ansible\'s collection structure.\n\nI should also verify that the playbook adheres to yamllint and ansible-lint standards, so I\'ll check for proper spacing, no trailing spaces, and correct use of colons and commas.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll start with \'---\', then list each task in the specified order, ensuring that conditions and module parameters are correctly applied. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations, keeping the YAML clean and only including the necessary tasks.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure all tasks are present, in the right order, and that each uses the correct modules and parameters as per the user\'s instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Task 2: Check if the ansible_pkg_mgr is set to apt and then manage automatic service management based on the apt_autostart_state variable\n  block:\n    - name: Check ansible_pkg_mgr and manage services\n      ansible.builtin.command: systemctl enable --now {{ item }}\n      when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'apt\'\n      with_items: \n        - "{{ apt_autostart_state }}"\n  vars:\n    ansible_python_interpreter: /usr/bin/python3\n\n- name: Task 3: Use the copy module to create the policy-rc.d file with the content "exit 101" and mode "755" if the apt_autostart_state is set to disabled\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    content: "exit 101"\n    dest: /usr/libexec/policy-rc.d\n    mode: \'755\'\n  when: apt_autostart_state == \'disabled\'\n\n- name: Task 4: Use the file module to remove the policy-rc.d file if the apt_autostart_state is set to enabled\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    state: absent\n  when: apt_autostart_state == \'enabled\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T09:19:25.187624021Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15840692869, 'load_duration': 98994104, 'prompt_eval_count': 396, 'prompt_eval_duration': 103037773, 'eval_count': 891, 'eval_duration': 15637188927, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--cdd6e308-4598-46b2-9c31-db14d0b8a80e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 396, 'output_tokens': 891, 'total_tokens': 1287}
