it, I should enclose the entire command in quotes or use a list.\n\nSo the correct way is:\n\ncommand:\n  cmd: \'echo "Playbook completed successfully"\'\n\nOr:\n\ncommand:\n  cmd:\n    - echo\n    - \'Playbook completed successfully\'\n\nBut in the original playbook, it\'s written as a single string without quotes around \'echo\', which would cause the parser to see \'echo\' as a separate argument. So that\'s a syntax error.\n\nAh, that\'s the issue! The \'cmd\' is written as a string without enclosing quotes, causing the parser to see \'echo\' as a separate value. So the YAML parser sees \'echo\' as a key without a value, leading to a syntax error.\n\nSo to fix it, I need to enclose the entire command in double quotes. Let me adjust that in the playbook.\n</think>\n\nThe error occurs because the `cmd` field in the final task is not properly quoted, causing the YAML parser to interpret it as multiple values. By enclosing the command in double quotes, we fix the syntax issue.\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install Keepalived when HA mode is enabled\n  apt:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  when: ha_mode\n\n- name: Download and install RKE2 {{ rke2_version }}\n  rke2_binary:\n    version: "{{ rke2_version }}"\n    install: true\n\n- name: Apply CIS Benchmark hardening for RKE2\n  template:\n    src: cis-hardening.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/rke2/cis-hardening.conf\n  command:\n    cmd: /usr/local/bin/rke2-cis-benchmark.sh --apply\n\n- name: Find the active server in the cluster\n  command:\n    cmd: kubectl get pods -A | grep -oE \'active\' | wc -l\n  register: active_server_count\n\n- name: Enable IPVS kernel module\n  sysctl:\n    name: net.ipv4.vs衙行\n    value: 1\n    persist: true\n\n- name: Copy kube-vip manifests to the masternode\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/kube-vip-manifests\n    dest: /etc/rke2/addons/kube-vip/\n    remote_src: true\n\n- name: Copy ingress-nginx manifests to the masternode\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/ingress-nginx-manifests\n    dest: /etc/rke2/addons/ingress-nginx/\n    remote_src: true\n\n- name: Prepare the very first server node in the cluster\n  rke2_node_prepare:\n    node: control_plane: true\n\n- name: Restore etcd specific tasks\n  rke2_etcd_restore:\n    restore_type: "{{ restore_type }}"\n\n- name: Download kubeconfig to ansible localhost\n  fetch:\n    src: /etc/rke2/kubeconfig\n    dest: /path/to/local/kubeconfig\n    flat: true\n\n- name: Prepare and join remaining nodes of the cluster\n  rke2_node_join:\n    node: ""\n\n- name: Rolling cordon and drain restart when version changes - servers\n  rke2_node_prepare:\n    rolling: true\n    role: server\n    version: "{{ rke2_version }}"\n\n- name: Rolling cordon and drain restart when version changes - agents\n  rke2_node_prepare:\n    rolling: true\n    role: agent\n    version: "{{ rke2_version }}"\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n\n- name: Perform rolling restart of cluster nodes when configuration files change\n  rke2_config_change:\n    config_path: /etc/rke2/config.yaml\n\n- name: Final steps\n  command:\n    cmd: \'echo "Playbook completed successfully"\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-22T10:11:40.946592667Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 143678595799, 'load_duration': 94654361, 'prompt_eval_count': 1362, 'prompt_eval_duration': 16987374, 'eval_count': 5991, 'eval_duration': 143564824674, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--d3877bc6-703c-448f-9ff8-c07bc7314008-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1362, 'output_tokens': 5991, 'total_tokens': 7353}
